<section class="section-black" id="your-clean"><div class="wrap">
<h2>How your Donaghadee bin clean works</h2>
<div class="grid">
<article class="card"><h3>1. Check your address</h3><p>Enter your postcode and address when booking. The available first-clean date is based on collection information and our cleaning rounds, so check the date shown for your property.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>2. Leave your bins accessible</h3><p>Have the bins you booked emptied and accessible after collection. You do not need to wait at home if we can reach them. We wash bins; we do not collect or remove rubbish.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>3. Wash, sanitise and deodorise</h3><p>We remove residue and grime, then sanitise and deodorise your bins. Regular cleaning helps keep waste residue and lingering smells from building up between visits.</p></article>
</div>
<h3>Black, blue, brown and green wheelie bins</h3>
<p>Book the bins your household uses, including general waste, recycling and garden or food-waste bins. Choose your bin colour in the form rather than assuming every bin at your property is included.</p>
<div class="bin-images"><figure><img src="/bins/120L.webp" alt="120 litre wheelie bin" width="150" height="130" loading="lazy"><figcaption>120 litre</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="/bins/240L.webp" alt="240 litre wheelie bin" width="150" height="130" loading="lazy"><figcaption>240 litre</figcaption></figure><figure><img src="/bins/360L.webp" alt="360 litre wheelie bin" width="150" height="130" loading="lazy"><figcaption>360 litre</figcaption></figure></div>
<p>Between visits, keep the lid closed and avoid leaving loose waste or leaking bags in your bin. Our <a href="/guides/how-to-stop-wheelie-bin-smells-and-maggots">guide to reducing bin smells and maggots</a> has more practical tips.</p>
</div></section>
<section class="section-dark" id="questions"><div class="wrap"><h2>Donaghadee bin cleaning questions</h2><div class="grid"><article class="card"><h3>How much is wheelie bin cleaning in Donaghadee?</h3><p>Regular domestic cleaning is £5 per bin per clean on our 4-weekly schedule. A one-off domestic clean is £15 per bin. Select your bins in the booking form to see your total before confirming.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>When will my bins be cleaned?</h3><p>Cleaning is arranged around bin collection and our local cleaning rounds. Enter your address and postcode in the booking form to check the available first-clean date. The 4-weekly service repeats every four weeks; it is not a weekly collection service.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>Which wheelie bins can I book?</h3><p>You can book black, blue, brown and green domestic wheelie bins. Choose the colour and quantity of each bin when booking, including multiple bins of the same colour.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>Do I need to be at home?</h3><p>You do not need to be home if your empty bins are out and accessible. Leave the bins you booked available after collection so we can reach them.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>Can I book a one-off clean instead?</h3><p>Yes. Choose the one-off option for a domestic clean at £15 per bin. Choose the 4-weekly option if you want a recurring cleaning schedule.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>Do you clean commercial bins in Donaghadee?</h3><p>Yes. We clean business bins and larger commercial containers by arrangement. Tell us the bin size, quantity and address so we can confirm the service and price.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>Do you empty bins or remove rubbish?</h3><p>No. This is a bin washing service, not rubbish collection. Your bins need to be emptied before cleaning.</p></article>
<article class="card"><h3>How do I manage an existing booking?</h3><p>Existing customers can use Customer HQ on our website to view their cleaning information. For help with your service, call 07555 178484 or email info@nibing.uy.</p></article></div></div></section>
